\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Analytic continuation in time}
\date{2026-11-13}

\p{Real time continues to Euclidean time by #{t=\ui\tau}: on the
half-plane #{\operatorname{Im}t>0} for the ground state, and on the
strip #{0<\operatorname{Im}t<\beta} at inverse temperature #{\beta}.
At #{t=\ui\tau} the vacuum factor #{\ue^{\ui t(H-E_0)}} equals
the semigroup factor #{\ue^{-\tau(H-E_0)}}. The thermal identity
##{C_\beta(A,B;\ui\tau)
 =Z_\beta^{-1}\trace(\ue^{-(\beta-\tau)H}A\ue^{-\tau H}B)}
follows from the real-time trace by cyclicity, for
#{0<\tau<\beta}. The time axis is a line: it has no unit
bivector of a plane and no central pseudoscalar of square #{-1}.}
